Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:34:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Safety rounds: unique event IDs, lifecycle rules and
 validated checkpoint PATCH

- Safety event and finding IDs use a uuid suffix instead of second-resolution
  timestamp + hash/count. Two checkpoints failed in the same second (or a
  round restarted within a second) raised IntegrityError -> HTTP 500 after the
  finding had already been written.
- Round lifecycle is enforced (HTTP 409 otherwise):
  start: PLANNED/OVERDUE -> IN_PROGRESS; complete/cancel: from PLANNED,
  IN_PROGRESS or OVERDUE; checkpoints can only be changed while the round is
  open. Cancelled/completed rounds can no longer be restarted or edited.
- Checkpoint PATCH uses a Pydantic model (SafetyCheckpointPatch) instead of a
  raw dict: invalid status/severity -> 422, omitted fields keep their value.
- Tests: tests/test_safety_round_rules.py.

